From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stuart Fraser <60394096+stuart902@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:29:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] power: reset: Add Apple D2365 shutdown and restart
 preparation

Run D2365 normal shutdown transactions in sleepable sys-off preparation.
Keep explicit managed links to same-PMIC GPIO and supply providers,
reject unbinding suppliers during probe and keep the atomic final
callback free of I2C operations. Refresh paired GPIO bytes before
writing, report uncertain standby transactions and keep ordinary reboot
preparation separate from conditional shutdown restart bookkeeping.

The existing watchdog performs reset. Linux source checks, failure
policy and bounded waiting are adaptations, not identical Apple
behavior. Hardware observations do not prove electrical power-off or the
final executed path.

[Orchard: from stuart902/linux 778174c50d5fd6b36849f9eea728a6811b1b6e9e;
consolidated export, production source unchanged.]

Assisted-by: LLM
